    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) headline our lineup, offering the most robust combination of favorable matchups and efficiency. **Jackson Merrill** benefits from a strong park factor and a soft matchup against Littell, and while the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time is a slight concern for his stolen base potential, his underlying power-speed profile remains elite. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is similarly well-positioned against Canning; his dynamic platoon advantage and current high-order placement make him a core building block for our Roto output. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Kyle Tucker** follow closely behind, with **Gunnar Henderson** receiving a significant boost from a park factor that helps offset his matchup against the tough Miles. **Sam Antonacci** is our highest-leverage play relative to his baseline, as his top-of-the-order status and an impressive xwOBA of 0.379 against Montero demand a start in the outfield.\n\nOur utility spot presents the tightest decision, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.95) falling just shy of the \"Strong\" start threshold due to a daunting matchup against Bradish. He narrowly edged out our other reserves, as the bench remains depleted by the ongoing absences of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Drake Baldwin**. **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung** round out our playable infielders with marginal-to-strong scores, leveraging favorable SP skill ratings to maintain their spots despite modest baseline projections. We are monitoring the risk inherent in **Liam Hicks** and **Brayan Rocchio**, who both sit near the 43-point mark; **Liam Hicks** survives in the lineup primarily due to wind conditions favoring hitters, while **Brayan Rocchio** remains a low-floor play in the #9 spot necessitated by our current roster constraints. Owners should keep a close watch on weather flags in these specific venues, as any late-breaking shifts could push **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Liam Hicks** into the bench category to preserve valuable game caps for later in the week.",
